abstract: >-
  MaxEnt Studio Pro is an open-source, full-stack computational GIS suite
  designed to modernize Maximum Entropy (MaxEnt) presence-only spatial modeling.
  It addresses key operational bottlenecks of legacy software by providing:
  (1) automated in-memory affine snapping and bilinear reprojection for
  multi-gigabyte GeoTIFF stacks (up to 2 GB), eliminating raster extent mismatch
  crashes; (2) a dual-engine architecture supporting both the headless official
  AMNH maxent.jar (v3.4.4) and a native pure-Python Scikit-Learn compatible
  L-BFGS solver with hinge, quadratic, and product feature expansions; (3)
  integrated presence-only validation metrics including the Continuous Boyce
  Index (CBI) and True Skill Statistic (TSS); and (4) an interactive Leaflet/Folium
  satellite web GIS interface with real-time decision cutoff filtering and
  single-click publication-ready GIS exports.
